    }

    .faq-item {
      background: #ffffff;
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
      border-radius: 14px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      overflow: hidden;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.02);
    }

    .faq-question {
      padding: 18px 22px;
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: 700;
      cursor: pointer;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .faq-question::after {
      content: "+";
      font-size: 22px;
      font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--gold);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }

    .faq-item.active .faq-question::after {
      content: "−";
    }

    .faq-answer {
      display: none;
      padding: 0 22px 22px;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
    }

    .faq-item.active .faq-answer {
      display: block;
    }

    .roam-morocco-bridge {
      background: #000000;
      color: #ffffff;
      padding: 40px 32px;
      margin: 50px 0;
      border-radius: 20px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(200, 164, 92, 0.45);
      box-shadow: 0 16px 48px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    }

    .roam-morocco-bridge h3 {
      color: #ffffff;
      font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);
      margin: 0 0 14px 0;
    }

    .roam-morocco-bridge p {
      color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
      font-size: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .bridge-cta-btn {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      background: var(--gold, #C8A45C);
      color: #000000 !important;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 13px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .06em;
      padding: 14px 28px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      text-decoration: none !important;
      transition: all 0.2s ease;
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif;
    }

    .bridge-cta-btn:hover {
      background: #ffffff;
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
  
  </style>

  <!-- Main Article -->
  <article class="article-wrap">

    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="roam-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/index.html">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/blog.html">Blog</a> &gt; <span>Where to Stay in Istanbul (2026)</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="category-badge">GLOBAL INTELLIGENCE &amp; IMPERIAL CROSSROADS</span>
      <h1 class="article-title">Where to Stay in Istanbul (2026): Sultanahmet vs Karaköy vs Kadıköy &amp; Bosphorus Guide</h1>
      <p class="article-subtitle">The essential neighborhood guide to the city spanning two continents. From Byzantine palaces in Sultanahmet to neo-bistros in Karaköy, seaside ferries in Kadıköy, and Ottoman waterfront mansions along the Bosphorus.</p>
      
      <div class="meta-bar">
        <span>🗓️ UPDATED: <strong class="gold-accent">OCTOBER 2026</strong></span>
        <span>⏱️ 17 MIN READ</span>
        <span>✍️ ROAM MOROCCO EDITORS</span>
        <span>📍 ISTANBUL, TURKEY</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero Figure -->
    <figure class="article-hero-fig">
      <img src="/images/istanbul-bosphorus-hero.jpg" alt="Panoramic golden hour sunset over the Bosphorus Strait, historic passenger ferry, and minarets of Hagia Sophia in Istanbul" width="1280" height="720">
      <figcaption>Dusk over the Golden Horn: historic Şehir Hatları ferry gliding past Hagia Sophia and the Blue Mosque minarets.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <div class="article-body">

      <p>Istanbul is not merely a crossroads between Europe and Asia; it is a colossal living tapestry of Roman, Byzantine, and Ottoman civilizations spanning two continents and two inland seas. Divided by the serpentine blue waters of the <strong>Bosphorus Strait</strong> and the historic inlet of the <strong>Golden Horn</strong>, choosing where to lay your head in this 16-million-person metropolis is the single most consequential decision you will make.</p>

      <p>Stay too far south in Sultanahmet, and you may find yourself marooned at 9:00 PM among shuttered carpet stores and overpriced tourist kebab houses. Stay too deep in Taksim, and you may find your sleep shattered by pounding nightclub bass until 4:00 AM. But choose your neighborhood strategically, and Istanbul reveals its incomparable magic: waking to the haunting sunrise call to prayer echoing across the water, sipping tulip-glass black tea as sea gulls follow the public ferries, and dining on mezze in ancient stone cellars.</p>

      <p>This 2026 field guide compares Istanbul's top four residential and travel districts, highlights curated boutique addresses, and reveals crucial airport transit and data connectivity hacks.</p>

