        <p>If your dream of Istanbul consists of walking out your hotel door and staring straight at the 1,500-year-old dome of <strong>Hagia Sophia</strong> or the six minarets of the <strong>Blue Mosque</strong>, Sultanahmet is unrivaled. Everything is within arm's reach: Topkapi Palace, the underground columns of the Basilica Cistern, the Hippodrome, and the labyrinthine vaulted corridors of the Grand Bazaar (Kapalıçarşı).</p>

