      <h2>5. Istanbul Airport (IST &amp; SAW) Transit Hacks</h2>

      <p>Istanbul is served by two major international airports. Knowing your airport transit route prevents expensive mistakes:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Istanbul Airport (IST) — The Main European Gateway (35 km Northwest):</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>M11 Driverless Metro Line (Fastest):</strong> Connects IST Airport to Gayrettepe station in just 30 minutes for approx. 30 TL (€0.90). At Gayrettepe, transfer to the M2 Green line directly into Taksim or Şişhane.</li>
            <li><strong>Havaist Express Buses:</strong> Luxury luggage-equipped coaches running every 20–30 minutes to Taksim, Beşiktaş, and Kadıköy for 180–220 TL (€5–€6). Clean, air-conditioned, and highly reliable.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Sabiha Gökçen Airport (SAW) — The Asian Side Hub:</strong> Connected to Kadıköy via the <strong>M4 Metro line</strong> in 50 minutes, or by Havabus express coach directly to Taksim Square.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--gold);">⚠️ Yellow Taxi Warning:</strong> Airport taxis in Istanbul are notorious for refusing to turn on taximeters, claiming "fixed tourist rates" of €60–€80, or driving longer roundabout routes. Insist on the meter (<em>"Taksimetre lütfen"</em>) or pre-book a verified private transfer through your hotel.</li>
      </ul>

